{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be","id":192951,"title":"What Kind of Uratha Would You Be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-09T18:34:44-07:00","id":192951,"title":"What Kind of Uratha Would You Be?","content":"If you were to wake up one day and undergo the First Change, what kind of Werewolf would you become? This thread is to tell the rest of us!<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's what you should put down, anything else is optional:<br /> <br /> Auspice<br /> <br /> Tribe<br /> <br /> Reason<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Ithaeur<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Bale Hound, masquerading as a Hunter in Darkness<br /> <br /> <b>Reason:</b> The world is F.U.B.A.R and most supernaturals would probably admit that. Those who don't are either blissfully naive humans, or still new to the World of Darkness. Everyone who's tried to fix the world has failed, either because they lacked the strength to carry it out, or became corrupted and lost sight of their goals. So why even bother attempting to fix a lost cause when joining the other side is so much more rewarding? I personally bare no ill will towards the Forsaken, I simply recognize that they're kidding themselves if they think they can make a difference.<br /> <br /> That being said, I can't just walk around shouting my true allegiances in full view of the public. I need someone to hide out with. And who better than the Hunters in Darkness, who are known for their privacy and don't take kindly to tresspassers? If I pretended to be one of them, then my irrational paranoia wouldn't seem all that suspicious by comparison! Of course I'd have to be really, really careful not to let them catch me tainting any of their land...<br /> <br /> As for my Auspice, I'm quite drawn to the allure of being able to wield magic, and when I was younger, I would attempt to scry visions out of obscure imagery from water stains, to stick piles, and even the creases in a wadded up dish cloth. The role of a shaman or an occultist would be suitable for me as an Uratha, plus all the delicious Gifts and powers I could obtain from the spirits would sweeten the deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T20:08:36-07:00","id":193045,"title":"","content":"*blows whistle*<br /> <br /> Boys, we got ourselves a twice-idiot!<br /> <br /> Thinks the Maeljin are any better, <i>and </i>put it in his profile!<br /> <br /> *sound of howling*<br /> <br /> As for me:<br /> <br /> <b>Auspice: </b>Ithaeur<br /> <br /> I'm a bookish, reserved sort with an angry streak, so that leads into a bookish, reserved werewolf. And likely lycanthropy induced first via finding something interesting and using it to better the world through shamanism, leading to the Lunes' reward via quickening the wolf-blooded genes (I've been reading the Idigam Chronicles spoilers, that seems like something that would result in the gift of Living Loci wolf blood), and from there First Change when something pisses me off enough to risk my life, which gets Luna's attention and decision to go all the way and get a new child out of the deal.<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe: </b>Bone Shadows.<br /> <br /> Again, bookish and reserved, these guys are my kind of wolves. That, and I really don't like violence; I doubt becoming a natural warrior would change that much. I prefer to ask the prey very nicely to go back to their world first, and offer carrot before stick. Doesn't mean I can't make their lives very miserable if they still insist on squatting on this side of the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T22:00:06-07:00","id":193130,"title":"","content":"No one should be one whit surprised by this.<br /> <br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Cahalith<br /> <br /> This recent Christmas holiday, the subject of DnD was on everyone's mind for some reason,as was assigning people classes. I was consistently told I was a bard-I have a way with words and emotions that apparently helps a lot of people out. Now a bard and a Cahalith are not the same-DnD Bards are sneakier bastards than Cahalith- but that is a score in the right direction. I am also, despite my darkling nature, a significant presence-I can sneak around when I want, don't get me wrong, I can go unnoticed-but when I'm not trying, I tend to subtly fill a room when I enter, and when I go for attention, I expand the room and grab everyone's attention. I also don't readily back down in arguments or in fights-I may mediate and try to avoid that(some Elodoth tendencies there), but more often than not that's a result of me being convinced I'm right and assuming a fight doesn't change the fact. I have been told that when I invest I am tenacious. I love stories, both the old ones and new ones I make up, and I love them in all their forms. I love music and often wish I could sing or play an instrument or dance well. On both fronts, it's because I have things that I want to say, that I want to rip out of me and into the world. I love glory and seek fame and communal recognition <i>a lot</i>. I love the Cahalith because they feel so damn familiar to me-in fact, it's one of the two x-splats that perfectly sum me up (the other being the Acanthus, namely the original, but certainly FWC's take isn't that far off either). I love them and play them because they are who I am.<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe: </b>Iron Masters<br /> <br /> Now remember when I said bards are sneaky bastards in DnD, and that that very much applied to me? Never let me talk. Br just confirmed it. As loud as I can be, it must be pointed out <i>I am not a nice person who plays by the rules</i>. I and sneaky,devious bastard-as a kid if I couldn't get you upfront, I'd wait until you were in a compromising position and then get you, like waiting until you were buckled and unable to move while the teacher was walking away before I'd pummel the shit out of you. That hasn't changed as an adult-in fact, it's gotten worse, because I tend to talk people into those compromising positions. Part of the reason I can do that is an absolute lack of care about the worth of my word-it doesn't matter to me if I told you I'll do something, it only matters to me if I care to do it. Again, I <i>cheat</i>. I <i>lie</i>. I reject just about anything that limits me, and if I can do so and make you think it will, all the better-your misconceptions are your problems unless I decide otherwise. I adapt by accepting very little as constant and running with what's handed to me. That's part of the reason I love cultures as much as I do-there are cores that remain constant, threads that bear out, but there's also rapidly changing movements and events and attitudes and thoughts. Society is a living tapestry, a flowing ocean of connections that shift and stay the same and just keep going. THe entire Slenderman thing was fascinating to watch, the birth of a new urban legend, and seeing how people bore that out, how it just shift and was hammered until we have the loose stories of today-who knows where that'll be years from now, and that's just an example. I like history a lot, because you can see how that shift happen, but here and now is where that same sort of thing is happening, and despite all we know we can't see fully where it's going. And as a final point, I both love and hate people. People are both glorious and pitiful, of constant shades of glamour and shame to them. I can see the amazing things everyone is capable of, and get frustrated at seeing them keep themselves from it, and i am both enraptured and horrified when they get over that tendency, with thecrazy ass things we create that threaten to improve the world and promise to end it. Again, I play Iron Masters because it's really familiar to me, I love and play them they are who I am.<br /> <br /> And in fact, of all the possible configurations throughout the lines I could be, I think it's this mix that hits the closest to who I am. If I existed in the World of Darkness as a supernatural, I would probably be a Cahalith Iron Master, despite all other options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T01:12:15-07:00","id":193275,"title":"","content":"Cahalith, Blood Talon.<br /> <br /> As a student of anthropology and a passion for the old Norse tales, what better then the historian Cahalith for THE GLORIOUS TRIBE OF FENRIS!?<br /> <br /> The natural lodge being the &quot;lodge of the Einherjar.&quot;<br /> <br /> The monsterous nature of the Cahalith and the desire to instil fear into those I hunt settles the desire for brutality normally inherent with my rage at the state of humanity. Working retail hasn't done anything to quell that, and a midnight hunt against that wife beater, or the heroin dealer only adds to the growing glory of the beast of Carson.<br /> <br /> At times my anger with the world makes me think the Maeljin have it right, but my pride and glory status won't let that thought take hold. I won't be someones patsy. Let them create new epics about the creature that takes those with the darkest souls. I'll write it in my history books for future generations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T01:59:18-07:00","id":193304,"title":"","content":"It's very hard to answer this question lacking the experience of being hunted by creatures who kill me if they catch me. Blood Talon, if they will have me. The choice of auspice isn't up to me - no reason to speculate. I cannot entirely rule out the possibility that the Predator Kings will be able to make me one of their own - they're very good at what they Do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T02:20:02-07:00","id":193308,"title":"","content":"<b>Auspice:</b> Irraka<br /> Now, this is of course presuming that the Change will take me based on my personality, and not by the whims of a mad goddess, or perhaps some prophetic vision about what I could be shaped into. But I know I'm fairly clever, and good at thinking outside the box, I also don't enjoy direct challenges. Irraka would fit there. The other choice is Cahalith, I'm triggering rather closely to the &quot;artistic&quot; stereotype of them, as a writer/Storyteller/story teller/and comfortable liar if it makes things simpler, or simply more interesting.<br /> <b>Tribe: </b>Bone Shadows or Iron Masters<br /> Both are intellectual and curious at their core. I love learning, so I'd fit well into the more introspective part of the Iron Masters, as well as mainline Bone Shadows. Call me stupid or credulous but I believe in ghosts, and have had quite a few events where that seems like the easiest explanation, and it's something I'm really curious about. Thus I lean more towards Bone Shadows, but the Iron Masters isn't written out completely. I suppose it depends on what kind of people the local tribe members are, and who I feel more comfortable with. <br /> <b>Lodge: </b>Death if Bone Shadows,<br /> Scrolls if Iron Master<br /> This is pretty much an extension of the Tribe part. Going further along the lines, to my focus-areas. Doesn't really need to be any more complicated than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T03:30:57-07:00","id":193364,"title":"","content":"<b>Auspice:</b> Elodoth<br /> <br /> Among my close ones, i tend to be seen as a mediator of some kind. It's ironic, because i'm one of the most un-balanced persons i know. But the thing is, i feel it. I feel how much far away i am from balance. I have this feeling deep inside me. Constantly. I think that's what my people see in me, the reason they usually involve me in their decisions about other persons. They feel my thrive to reach balance. I don't achieve it, but nonetheless i try. And the trying keep me focused on it,and allows me to share my -particular- vision of balance with them. <br /> <br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Storm Lords. Well. Dead-would-be Storm Lord, most probably.<br /> <br /> If there's a motto i identify with, it's theirs. Improve or die. Grow by facing your weaknesses. Fight against yourself. To be self-reliant. To thrive. I cannot express it with fancy words, I can only feel it... and i feel it deep in the bones. Now, i know i'm not enough for them, but if i were to be one of the member of the Tribes of the Moon, i know i'd rather die than stop trying to become one of them. So, yes. Iminir.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:08:25-07:00","id":193398,"title":"","content":"<b>Auspice</b>: None. I have no need of Luna's gifts. <br /> <br /> <b>Tribe</b>: Ivory claws. <br /> <br /> The murder of father wolf and the loss of Pangaea has left the world in a unnatural state. Its only right that we tear the walls down and create a united world once more. Sure a spirit might kill a human or two but hey you can't make an omelette without breaking a few eggs. Of course the world is gong to need leaders when its all over. And again its only natural that it should be us. <br /> <br /> <b>Lodge</b>: council of eagles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:27:59-07:00","id":193409,"title":"","content":"<b>Auspice</b>: Rahu. I like punching my problems away<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe</b>: Iron masters<br /> <br /> I just have a compulsion to ask &quot;Why?&quot; , that and 2 words: awakened IPAD &gt;: D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T07:48:00-07:00","id":193561,"title":"","content":"<b>Auspice</b>: Cahalith (Could go with Irraka as well, but I tend to gravitate towards people more than my loner tendencies)<br /> <b>Tribe</b>: Hunter in Darkness<br /> <br /> Interesting that my Primary Werewolf character is a Cahalith Lorekeeper of the Hunters in Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T08:25:10-07:00","id":193642,"title":"","content":"<b>Irraka </b>- I tend to play my cards close to the vest. I'd rather handicap my opponents that do anything like a &quot;fair fight&quot; (I think it's a BS term, anyway). I'm fine being on my own for a while, but I do come back to the family when they need me or I need them. I am not above using &quot;dirty tactics&quot; to win (again, I don't always agree that they are). I'd rather think, trick and escape than just bully my way out of something.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Master</b> - I love watching the world change and trying to keep up with it while also tracking how far it's gone from where it started. I very nearly pursued an archaeology/anthropology degree. And I have a tendency to ask &quot;Why?&quot; before anything else. One of my former managers was ex-military and he said I'd make a lousy soldier because if he yelled &quot;Duck!&quot;, my reflexive reaction would be to ask &quot;Why?&quot; instead of ducking. I couldn't disagree with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 07-10-2014, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T08:48:35-07:00","id":193669,"title":"","content":"<b>Ithaeur.</b> I'm reserved, I have a very curious and inquiring mind and I like to read and solve puzzles. I'm usually the quiet one in a group unless I know something that is relevant to the conversation or I have an idea, at which point I can barely keep my mouth shut.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter in Darkness.</b> Walking along an undeveloped, unpaved place is a huge stress reliever for me. I love camping, and I don't get to do it nearly as much as I would like. If I can turn into a wolf, how much camping gear would I even need?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T10:29:15-07:00","id":193760,"title":"","content":"Tribe: StormLord. My whole life has been about surviving the worst in life. All the while making sure those around me never gave up on whatever they were going through. I was strong for them when they couldn't be.<br /> <br /> Elodoth: Everything must be in balance. If not chaos and disorder run rampant.<br /> <br /> Lodge: Lodge of the Savior. I would live my life balancing my beliefs in my faith with those of the Litany.<br /> <br /> I wear my tribal allegiance in ink on my shoulder. and my lodge on my arm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T12:47:49-07:00","id":193863,"title":"","content":"<b>Auspice</b>: Rahu<br /> <br /> I Rage. I see injustice, and I cannot enact justice. I see tyranny, and I cannot rebel. Whether acting on violent impulses is simply inappropriate, or I lack the strength to enact my will, I yearn for wrathful release. My Rage would be glorious to behold, and I would revel in it.<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe</b>: Iron Masters<br /> <br /> My least favorite excuse for anything is &quot;Tradition for tradition's sake...&quot;. It is stagnation and fear and an unwillingness to accept that there is something <i>wrong</i> with the world. Or it is sloth. And thus I would join the Tribe willing to change, willing to adapt, willing to accept that things are broken and who are willing to fix them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T15:06:01-07:00","id":194000,"title":"","content":"<b>Auspice: </b>Elodoth<br /> I obsess over keeping things as objective as possible with an assumption that i might always be wrong to help me keep from being haughty. A quote that really influenced me in my childhood was &quot;A wise person is one who knows that they know nothing&quot; said by Plato (who might have been quoting Socrates). I haven't always followed it (i'm pretty sure Pride is my Vice) but it has formed how i have tried to live my life up to this point even though it can give me the image of truly not knowing anything. Since there is always something to learn there is nothing that can be said to be proven 100% and so one must entertain Doubt in every decisions.<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe: </b>Hunters of Darkness<br /> With a sense of stability and tradition, being a member of the Tribe that attempts to uphold the Forsaken Values and traditions seems a natural choice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T16:30:13-07:00","id":194092,"title":"","content":"<b>Auspice</b>: Cahalith<br /> I was born during a Waning Gibbous (<i>Moon Phase</i>). I love to find/learn things and then tell people about what I know or found. I'm definitely a lorekeeper in the subjects I'm into (<i>Books, books, and more books</i>!). I also enjoy helping people. But I'm also very passionate and sometimes I can be blunt when describing things to others (<i>stems from being a visual learner foremost</i>). I also draw, doodle, sculpt, bake, make, and enjoy creating things. I'll probably be into creating fetishes/items for use for my fellow packmates and trying to help out with what I can.<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Hunters in Darkness<br /> I find it much easier to communicate with animals than I do with people (<i>Even if I'm getting over that as I age, I'm still shy or have problems in certain social situations</i>. <i>As I kid, I used to fear having to talk on the phone.</i>). I can also can easily navigate and memorize anything doing with spatial memory/space, so I can easily figure out my location and where to go. I'm territorial and I like it when I can have a few moments to be alone by myself. I like being outside and observing nature. But I really dislike it when someone disrespects a serenity/sense of a place (<i>Graffiti over old petroglyphs or art murals for example</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T12:03:31-07:00","id":194866,"title":"","content":"Auspice: None<br /> <br /> Tribe: Fire-Touched.<br /> <br /> Reason: Well hello bitch-pups of Mother Moon! Would you like to take the time to hear about our savior Gurim-Ur? You don't? That is a real shame. Tell you what- I'll give you a few days to think it over, maybe I'll burn your house and family to ashes and give you the equivalent of spirit-ebola, so I'll see you soon!<br /> <br /> Lodge: Lodge of Fevered Light","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-11-2014, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T16:20:24-07:00","id":195096,"title":"","content":"What is it with you people and antagonist groups?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:04:04-07:00","id":195112,"title":"","content":"The Bale Hounds are pretty neat, as far as antagonists go, and while the Forsaken and Pure experiences are broad, they aren't all-encompassing in terms of things people want to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T18:34:03-07:00","id":195172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195096#post195096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is it with you people and antagonist groups?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, the world is beyond fixing!<br /> <br /> <br /> And Nofather is right. The Bale Hounds seem to have a broader sense of goals than just &quot;Guide the humans&quot; vs &quot;Fuck the humans&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T18:59:45-07:00","id":195181,"title":"","content":"Auspice: Cahalith.<br /> <br /> Constant reading, constant writing, constant telling and sharing of stories. I love history and narrative, and I think being able to cling onto something like mythology after the trauma of the First Change and being confronted with this new life would be soothing indeed. Not everyone can go out and slaughter the Pure and reason with the spirits; there's something very human about talking around the fire and chatting all through the night. Pity about the dreams; they're bad enough without Luna stepping in.<br /> <br /> Tribe: Ghost Wolf.<br /> <br /> I'm too soft to be a Blood Talon, too blind to be a Bone Shadow, too fond of cities and the light to be a Hunter in Darkness, and the Storm Lords just set me on edge. Someone might be able to teach me how to be an Iron Master, but I've got no skills for them just yet. The idea of tribe freaks me out anyway; I've got no connection to these ancient groups, and don't really have any desire to hob aboard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T19:26:07-07:00","id":195197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195172#post195172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, the world is beyond fixing!</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.authorama.com/fables-16.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.authorama.com/files/authors/robert-l-stevenson.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.authorama.com/fables-16.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Fables - XVII. - Faith, Half Faith and No Faith At All. (by Robert Louis Stevenson) </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.authorama.com/fables-16.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.authorama.com/fables-16.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The complete text of Fables </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T19:44:44-07:00","id":195201,"title":"","content":"If the world was beyond fixing, there'd be no one to point it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T20:46:30-07:00","id":195225,"title":"","content":"Auspice: Ithaeur<br /> Tribe: Bale Hound<br /> <br /> Ithaeur because I'm inquisitive and curious, the temptation of dangerous knowledge is irresistable, and were the world of spirits to open up before my I would probably find it comfy as a second home.<br /> <br /> Bale Hound is really one of the most appealing of options to me. All three of versions offered up are great, whether it's swearing oneself to one of the Maeljin, worshipping them all in a fanaticized dark pantheism with the hopes of joining them as a maeladar one day, or making a vow to Viruhk-Ur and promoting the desires of all the Maeljin while also disrupting the balance of the Forsaken and the Pure.<br /> <br /> I'd pick the latter, Bale Hound as tribe. While I find the Pure to be good villains, especially the Fire-Touched (I'm really curious about the theory of religion as communicable mental illness, and was pleased to see someone would join the Fevered Light lodge), their goal of engulfing the world in the Shadow is just something I'm not interested in. The Forsaken themselves, while playing them more, are really setting themselves up to a life of juggling acts, balancing the wants of spirits and the intrusions of humanity and all the various things that could smash through their carefully cultivated territories like wrecking balls.<br /> <br /> The Bale Hounds get to be those wrecking balls. And they don't even have to do it personally. All it takes is a suggestion, a nod, a signature on a paper. Someone lies or cheats, someone throws a punch, the spiritual landscape shifts to accomodate a powerful new law. While I see where Nyrufa is coming from, I don't believe the world is fixing, or even needs fixing. The world is what it is. And in the game, it's the World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> The Pure have an unachievable goal, the Forsaken take a character-building path that never ends and pit themselves against an endless number of enemies. But the Bale Hounds see the world for what it is and help nudge it along. In turn, they aren't the enemy of infinite spirits. In turn, the fruits of their labors can dot the landscape, marking their deeds in the world itself. In turn, they are part of something greater than them. And in turn, they're on the winning side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T21:18:30-07:00","id":195239,"title":"","content":"Look, not to use kid logic, but while I can understand the Pure a little bit, the Bale Hounds are so clearly <i>the bad guys</i>. I don't see how people can buy the logic of the bad guys. Their lies, sure, but not the logic. I'd rather be a Ghost Wolf than be a Bale Hound. <i> Hell</i>, I'd rather be in the Anshenga-even the Ivory Claws!-than be a Bale Hound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T22:14:09-07:00","id":195262,"title":"","content":"I can't post without at least ten letters, but:<br /> <br /> So?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T23:48:25-07:00","id":195301,"title":"","content":"The seven-year old in me is very clearly yelling &quot;You can't join the bad guys!&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T02:29:55-07:00","id":195342,"title":"","content":"Auspice: Cahilith, though I'm told Rahu fits very well.<br /> I'm a Cahilith, I've got a hundred different potential games, and characters all bubbling up. I've got a hard drive filled with poetry and the ruins of countless short stories and books I started and never finished. I play three different instruments, and though singing isn't one of them, drum and bass guitar both are. The pack of dogs I live with howl, grow, whine and talk to me, and more often then not the whines and howls I make back seem to placate them. I'll write the story of the hunt, and then howl its' glory, with the kill still fresh on in my mouth.<br /> <br /> Tribe: Storm Lord<br /> I could be nothing but Iminir. When those around me falter, I step to the fore, and if I have to I'll drag those behind me to greatness. I'm the leader, its a simple fact. Others worry about what they need to do, while I am concerned with how everyone is doing. I pick up the slack and cheerlead, urging everyone to do more and to do better. But, more than all this, I hold myself to a whole other level when I'm in charge. I refuse anything but my absolute best,because it is my example that others will follow. There is no failure, there is no weakness, only the glory to be earned in victory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T07:30:39-07:00","id":195494,"title":"","content":"Auspice: Rahu<br /> Tribe: Hunters in Darkness<br /> <br /> I would probably be a kind suspected Pure symphatizer due to my general dislike for humans and preference for the wilds, as well as often taken advantage of times when I could kill humans like forest workers and general urban people not treating the wilds very nicely when I could get away with it. No, I don't think that I would be a very, for humans, nice or pleasant individual. But since I wouldn't be eating humans or forsaking the Oath of the Moon, more than killing extra humans, I hope the Forsken could allow me to roll with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":". 07-12-2014, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T08:54:48-07:00","id":195555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195301#post195301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The seven-year old in me is very clearly yelling &quot;You can't join the bad guys!&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some men just want to watch the world burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T09:23:50-07:00","id":195566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195555#post195555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Some men just want to watch the world burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much it. While one person might not understand it, they haven't walked in the other persons shoes to know their views. I'm very much a StormLord but I could just as easily fall into the Bale Hounds. Honestly they scare me more than any Black Spiral ever did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T12:20:55-07:00","id":195655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195301#post195301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The seven-year old in me is very clearly yelling &quot;You can't join the bad guys!&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>MY inner seven-year old is clearly yelling &quot;Bad guys get the best musical numbers!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T13:00:10-07:00","id":195695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195096#post195096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is it with you people and antagonist groups?</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't you heard Arcane? Ladies love the dark scoundrels!<br /> <br /> My poor attempt at faux misogyny aside, antagonistic factions are fun because it's playing the game from the eyes of the &quot;enemy&quot;. World of Darkness is a game that shows that rarely are things black and white, and I love playing on the side which is shoehorned into the &quot;black&quot; side of the morality scale- all the better to show that the members of that faction are in fact people and not just monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T13:06:23-07:00","id":195698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195239#post195239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, not to use kid logic, but while I can understand the Pure a little bit, the Bale Hounds are so clearly <i>the bad guys</i>. I don't see how people can buy the logic of the bad guys. Their lies, sure, but not the logic. I'd rather be a Ghost Wolf than be a Bale Hound. <i> Hell</i>, I'd rather be in the Anshenga-even the Ivory Claws!-than be a Bale Hound.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will agree that Bale Hounds are an exception to my personal rules, but other than those who undoubtedly do evil for the sake of spreading evil, there are still many factions who are &quot;bad guys&quot;, yet still have the depth to be intriguing npcs or player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T13:14:46-07:00","id":195704,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I get that, and if this were a discussion about characters, I'd be on board.<br /> <br /> But we're talking about <i>what we think we'd be in this world</i>. I'm a little disturbed that there are people siding with the really screwed up side of things, that when presented with black and grey organizations, people are picking the black ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T13:35:28-07:00","id":195717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195704#post195704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I get that, and if this were a discussion about characters, I'd be on board.<br /> <br /> But we're talking about <i>what we think we'd be in this world</i>. I'm a little disturbed that there are people siding with the really screwed up side of things, that when presented with black and grey organizations, people are picking the black ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for me, I picked the Fire-Touched because I have very strong spiritual and religious views, so in light of that I chose the one tribe that is closest to my overall personality. It just happened to be a Pure Tribe lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T13:37:12-07:00","id":195718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195655#post195655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> MY inner seven-year old is clearly yelling &quot;Bad guys get the best musical numbers!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My inner seven year old is singing &quot;Be Prepared&quot; in a horrible imitation of Scar personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T14:14:39-07:00","id":195738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195704#post195704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we're talking about <i>what we think we'd be in this world</i>. I'm a little disturbed that there are people siding with the really screwed up side of things, that when presented with black and grey organizations, people are picking the black ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kinda surprised you feel that way. In your own entry you proudly describe yourself as a liar and a cheat who loves glory and fame and communal recognition and seek them out. As loud as can be, you state that 'I am not a nice person who plays by the rules,' and 'I reject just about anything that limits me.' Joining up with the Forsaken and denouncing Bale Hounds as 'bad guys - do not touch' seems like putting a needless restriction upon yourself.<br /> <br /> Besides that, it certainly sounds like you'd fit in with the Bale Hounds Perhaps not as a tribe or with the dark pantheism, but I wouldn't be surprised at a deal with one of the Maeljin. Lamashtu, the Maeljin of Pride, would probably be rewarding of the highly valuable services you could provide. You'd, likely, already be living a lie, as the Oaths of the Moon bind you to keep your true self from the herd, why wouldn't you put your already exercised skills of deceit to use and get something out of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T15:06:05-07:00","id":195781,"title":"","content":"Well, let me put it this way: do you think I'm a good person? Cause I know a lot of people think I am here.<br /> <br /> And for all my bleating about not being a nice person-which is absolutely true, by the way-I know I am far and away from being a <i>bad</i> person. And a lot of that is because I'm invested in being a good person-a good person who's not limited by arbitrary things, but a good person nonetheless. I have a flexible morality, sure, but that still means I have a morality. I'm just willing to constantly reappraise it, and have no problem basing things on the circumstances rather than something stricter. I don't like commandments, I like conscience.(Now wrap your head around the fact that I am an LDS Christian)<br /> <br /> Just about anything is not absolutely everything. Lines are needed-even the Iron Masters know this, and there's a reason something like the Idigam are huge ass problems. Are they perpetually needed? Depends on the situation, but for me as an individual there are less than most people think there should be. I want to do things because I care about them, but as a general rule, I care about being a good person. Just not a nice one, and fairly often I have no problem being a very rough person<br /> <br /> And while I am inherently something of a narcissist, I do care about other people. Yes, I really like praise and glory, and yes I will totally eat your sausages if I'm hungry or trick you out of your parachute and jump from the building in Betrayal at House On the Hill-but I I will also very likely buy you more sausage later to make it up later, and if you're upset over what I did in the game I will probably apologize for it. The important point, though, is that I don't do either because it's expected of me. If I'm required to, forget it. If it's demanded I do things to make up for them, I will reply with a hearty &quot;Go fuck yourself&quot;. But if you let me be myself? I generally fix what I break.(Plus, the way I've decided to get communal fame is through living strangely and writing, that should tell you a few things)<br /> <br /> THe big thing though? Big picture. I like the world. I have hope for the world. I think helping it along is great(and a good way to get myself fame too). I don't think the Maeljin promote a picture I'm invested in. I don't think the things I want are wanted badly enough I don't mind them being wrapped so blatantly in sin. The Deceiver might lightly appeal to me, but my lies are mine, not his, and I don't like what they do with it. The Pure aren't much better-their crusade is more understandable, but it's fueled by hate, and while I am deeply familiar with the emotion, I don't like it and would rather not live off of it.<br /> <br /> And broadly, I like the struggle the Forsaken have. I mean, yeah, it sucks. It really does. But it's going to a place I like, and it's not terrible actually, in the meanwhile. That's a contradiction. But it all comes down to is that the Forsaken live a life I can get behind, the sort of thing I care about. It's not perfect, but it's not bad.<br /> <br /> Plus you say &quot;get something out of it&quot; like I need to sign up with a demon to do so. I don't, thanks much.<br /> <br /> Or, simply: I'm just not interested in what the Bale Hounds and the Pure do enough to care what they can give me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, for clarity, consider that one of my two favorite Orders from Mage are the Guardians of the Veil. That should explain plenty.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, there's a difference between proudly and honestly. One thing I try not to do in my life is lie about who I am or excuse it. I'm not always successful, but it's one of those things I care about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-12-2014, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T16:19:23-07:00","id":195821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195704#post195704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I get that, and if this were a discussion about characters, I'd be on board.<br /> <br /> But we're talking about <i>what we think we'd be in this world</i>. I'm a little disturbed that there are people siding with the really screwed up side of things, that when presented with black and grey organizations, people are picking the black ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I've written off a lot of people on this forum after reading this thread. I'm probably going further than you, though.<br /> <br /> But I'd likely be a Storm Lord, so that isn't much of a surprise. So much weakness here, to take the easy path, to give in, to simper and abase oneself, to take pride in cowardliness. It's a sterling example of everything that's wrong with the world; of course they circularly reason that this is why they've done it in the first place.<br /> <br /> I'm almost surprised you guys don't pick Azlu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T17:42:21-07:00","id":195853,"title":"","content":"I've always found this sort of thread to be highly disturbing. What sort of person wants to be a werewolf? Not one who understands this game, nor anyone I would enjoy spending time with in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T17:50:05-07:00","id":195860,"title":"","content":"<b>Auspice:</b> Ithaeur<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Iron Masters<br /> <br /> I know myself well enough to understand that even if I have super powers I'd likely spend a good bit of my time reading books. I'd likely continue to try and understand the world around me, especially given how much more of the world I suddenly have access to. I wouldn't necessarily deny my instincts purposefully, but my intense self-scrutiny means I would still think like a human in many ways. The loss of control to Kuruth would horrify me to the core.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that I just plain like people and human culture in general. I'm hardly a shining beacon of what I naively call the Enlightenment, but I try to nurture its embers where I can. I would most likely take up a protective impulse towards the Herd in general, though I can't say I would be above culling it when necessary even if that would be the option I go to last. Curiosity would abound, I'd likely join the Lodge of Scrolls to continue my studies. <br /> <br /> Somewhere between Sherlock Holmes and Dr. Jekyll, but a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T18:06:36-07:00","id":195870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195781#post195781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, let me put it this way: do you think I'm a good person? Cause I know a lot of people think I am here.<br /> <br /> And for all my bleating about not being a nice person-which is absolutely true, by the way-I know I am far and away from being a <i>bad</i> person. And a lot of that is because I'm invested in being a good person-a good person who's not limited by arbitrary things, but a good person nonetheless. I have a flexible morality, sure, but that still means I have a morality. I'm just willing to constantly reappraise it, and have no problem basing things on the circumstances rather than something stricter. I don't like commandments, I like conscience.(Now wrap your head around the fact that I am an LDS Christian)<br /> <br /> Just about anything is not absolutely everything. Lines are needed-even the Iron Masters know this, and there's a reason something like the Idigam are huge ass problems. Are they perpetually needed? Depends on the situation, but for me as an individual there are less than most people think there should be. I want to do things because I care about them, but as a general rule, I care about being a good person. Just not a nice one, and fairly often I have no problem being a very rough person<br /> <br /> And while I am inherently something of a narcissist, I do care about other people. Yes, I really like praise and glory, and yes I will totally eat your sausages if I'm hungry or trick you out of your parachute and jump from the building in Betrayal at House On the Hill-but I I will also very likely buy you more sausage later to make it up later, and if you're upset over what I did in the game I will probably apologize for it. The important point, though, is that I don't do either because it's expected of me. If I'm required to, forget it. If it's demanded I do things to make up for them, I will reply with a hearty &quot;Go fuck yourself&quot;. But if you let me be myself? I generally fix what I break.(Plus, the way I've decided to get communal fame is through living strangely and writing, that should tell you a few things)<br /> <br /> THe big thing though? Big picture. I like the world. I have hope for the world. I think helping it along is great(and a good way to get myself fame too). I don't think the Maeljin promote a picture I'm invested in. I don't think the things I want are wanted badly enough I don't mind them being wrapped so blatantly in sin. The Deceiver might lightly appeal to me, but my lies are mine, not his, and I don't like what they do with it. The Pure aren't much better-their crusade is more understandable, but it's fueled by hate, and while I am deeply familiar with the emotion, I don't like it and would rather not live off of it.<br /> <br /> And broadly, I like the struggle the Forsaken have. I mean, yeah, it sucks. It really does. But it's going to a place I like, and it's not terrible actually, in the meanwhile. That's a contradiction. But it all comes down to is that the Forsaken live a life I can get behind, the sort of thing I care about. It's not perfect, but it's not bad.<br /> <br /> Plus you say &quot;get something out of it&quot; like I need to sign up with a demon to do so. I don't, thanks much.<br /> <br /> Or, simply: I'm just not interested in what the Bale Hounds and the Pure do enough to care what they can give me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, for clarity, consider that one of my two favorite Orders from Mage are the Guardians of the Veil. That should explain plenty.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, there's a difference between proudly and honestly. One thing I try not to do in my life is lie about who I am or excuse it. I'm not always successful, but it's one of those things I care about.</div> </div> </div> </div>And lots of people are nice, good people. Problem is, in the werewolf setting the nice, good people are often due for some very difficult decisions. I am often referred to as and think of myself as a rather kind and friendly person, but even the nice people can be drawn into the wrong crowd if they do not know there are alternatives. That's why I like to think that even though I would join the Fire-Touched ( because even though they are a Pure Tribe, they do have a number of noble aspects in addition to the hate based ones that I would agree with a first) , I would eventually defect and become a Ghost Wolf, because my natural compassion would eventually be at odds at what the Tribe demands of me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-12-2014, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T18:15:35-07:00","id":195887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195853#post195853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always found this sort of thread to be highly disturbing. What sort of person wants to be a werewolf? Not one who understands this game, nor anyone I would enjoy spending time with in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luckily, it is a work of fiction, so you don't have to worry about any of us hulking out and mauling you for little to no reason lol. That being said, let us pretend that you are one of the people who would want to be an Uratha- what is the Tribe/Auspice/Lodge you think you would most fit into?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T18:17:01-07:00","id":195888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195821#post195821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm almost surprised you guys don't pick Azlu.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Azlu are more like the Forsaken and Pure, attempting to do good for their mythological progenitor, but without the ties to humankind. I imagine most people wouldn't pick the Azlu because eating brains isn't looked upon as a thrill to most, and they're utterly inhuman. Bale Hounds are, conversely, very human, relishing in various aspects of humanity and werewolf both. A group like Belial's Brood involves playing a limbo game of 'how low can you go' with conventional morality, but a Bale Hound can just take advantage of the opportunities given to them, encouraging the vices of others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195781#post195781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, let me put it this way: do you think I'm a good person? Cause I know a lot of people think I am here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond your posts in this thread and your mention that you don't have the Blasphemies book in another, I don't know anything about you. But I don't tend to think of people as good or bad. You're a person, like everyone else. You're perfectly capable of doing good or bad things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T18:24:39-07:00","id":195895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195718#post195718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My inner seven year old is singing &quot;Be Prepared&quot; in a horrible imitation of Scar personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>We need a line of Bale Hounds marching under a cliff rocking out to this song.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T18:31:15-07:00","id":195900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195888#post195888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Beyond your posts in this thread and your mention that you don't have the Blasphemies book in another, I don't know anything about you. But I don't tend to think of people as good or bad. You're a person, like everyone else. You're perfectly capable of doing good or bad things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how not having Blasphemies factors into this other than the fact that he has less knowledge of the BH than others who do have the supplement, but I do see you point,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T18:34:57-07:00","id":195901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195853#post195853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always found this sort of thread to be highly disturbing. What sort of person wants to be a werewolf? Not one who understands this game, nor anyone I would enjoy spending time with in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it's just some fun. No one wants to live in the world of darkness, but if you suddenly found yourself there, certainly being one of the splats would make you better equipped to handle it. And while no one wants to be taken by True Fae and have a Durance, or be put together from disparate pieces and then have to go on a quest to develop a soul, if you were taken, or had to go on that quest because you didn't get a choice to, you may as well think about how you'd deal with it in that situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T19:37:20-07:00","id":195952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195821#post195821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I've written off a lot of people on this forum after reading this thread. I'm probably going further than you, though.<br /> <br /> But I'd likely be a Storm Lord, so that isn't much of a surprise. So much weakness here, to take the easy path, to give in, to simper and abase oneself, to take pride in cowardliness. It's a sterling example of everything that's wrong with the world; of course they circularly reason that this is why they've done it in the first place.<br /> <br /> I'm almost surprised you guys don't pick Azlu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not taking people too seriously here, or at least I'm working at not. It's just-it's less disturbing, more weird, that people choose to define themselves thusly. I still think really well of the people who have responded with joining &quot;el lado oscuro&quot;.<br /> <br /> @nofather:Sorry, I'm still used to when I was really freaking active on the forums and everyone used to know who I was. Granted, a lot of people here still know me pretty well, so..did I have a point here? Whatever.<br /> <br /> I have briefly read Blasphemies, but not enough to solidly know the particular lore it dishes on Bale Hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-12-2014, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T19:42:27-07:00","id":195953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195952#post195952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not taking people too seriously here, or at least I'm working at not. It's just-it's less disturbing, more weird, that people choose to define themselves thusly.<br /> <br /> @nofather:Sorry, I'm still used to when I was really freaking active on the forums and everyone used to know who I was. Granted, a lot of people here still know me pretty well, so..did I have a point here? Whatever.<br /> <br /> I have briefly read Blasphemies, but not enough to solidly know the particular lore it dishes on Bale Hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well here is one young man who still knows ya XD. But whether or not you have a point doesn't matter, you said what you wanted to say, and that is what is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T19:51:30-07:00","id":195955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195853#post195853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always found this sort of thread to be highly disturbing. What sort of person wants to be a werewolf? Not one who understands this game, nor anyone I would enjoy spending time with in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? If anything the Forsaken Werewolves seem like the most noble of all the playable archetypes. They're trying to prevent the utter and total fucking of the planet. Sure they've got a few anger management problems, but on the whole, they're putting their powers towards a good cause. Mages are selfish, Vampires are callous, Changelings are too busy trying to fit in. Werewolves are actually getting off their butts and doing something about these issues.","signature":"","edi