nchained and have MEGA AWESOME POWERS!<br /> <br /> Werewolf powers are cool too..<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">I guess... </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T00:34:51-07:00","id":196088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=196074#post196074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why be a Mage when you can be Unchained and have MEGA AWESOME POWERS!</div> </div> </div> </div>Flexibility when it comes to doing your job for starters.<br /> <br /> The retirement package is also pretty competitive to boot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T00:50:27-07:00","id":196095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195821#post195821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I've written off a lot of people on this forum after reading this thread. I'm probably going further than you, though.<br /> <br /> But I'd likely be a Storm Lord, so that isn't much of a surprise. So much weakness here, to take the easy path, to give in, to simper and abase oneself, to take pride in cowardliness. It's a sterling example of everything that's wrong with the world; of course they circularly reason that this is why they've done it in the first place.<br /> <br /> I'm almost surprised you guys don't pick Azlu.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you're saying that you make your judgement on people based on what they write on a internet thread about fictional creatures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T07:07:48-07:00","id":196252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=195955#post195955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? If anything the Forsaken Werewolves seem like the most noble of all the playable archetypes. They're trying to prevent the utter and total fucking of the planet. Sure they've got a few anger management problems, but on the whole, they're putting their powers towards a good cause. Mages are selfish, Vampires are callous, Changelings are too busy trying to fit in. Werewolves are actually getting off their butts and doing something about these issues.</div> </div> </div> </div> The mythology isn't complete without both the hero and the monster archetype. And I don't want to be a monster.<br /> <br /> Think of it like this: I have never hit my wife before. There are times when I felt like doing so, because this is how relationships work, and they've been few, because this is how good relationships work, but it has never happened and will never happen.<br /> <br /> A werewolf in this sort of situation isn't tempted to hit his wife. He's probably doing what he can to resist a much stronger temptation to turn into 3 meters of raging wolf death, tear out the wife's throat and abdomen and devour her heart.<br /> <br /> I don't want to be that monster. I don't want people I love to be afraid of me. Anyone who wants to be something like that is severely misunderstanding much of what these games are about.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T09:39:51-07:00","id":196355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=196095#post196095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So you're saying that you make your judgement on people based on what they write on a internet thread about fictional creatures?</div> </div> </div> </div>I make my judgement on people based on what they write on an internet thread about themselves using fictional creatures as a proxy, yes. As ArcaneArts pointed out, if this were about <i>characters</i>, there wouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> I feel like I'm at a meeting of Sociopaths Anonymous. &quot;Last week I thought I'd find someone emotionally vulnerable and convince them to give in to their wrath. They nearly beat their partner to death. I watched. It was beautiful.&quot; I guess I could be more charitable in my interpretation and just find you all to be liars. Or I could apply Hanlon's Razor and decide you're all stupid. Do you have a preference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T11:03:01-07:00","id":196434,"title":"","content":"You know what, I wrote two different responses until I decided that its probably just a needless way to ge the mods pissed and so I'll walk away and not persue this discussion.<br /> <br /> Needless to say I still think that you are wrong in making judgement over people based on a single post on an internet forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":".  Decided to try and be a better man. 07-13-2014, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T11:37:30-07:00","id":196497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=196355#post196355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I make my judgement on people based on what they write on an internet thread about themselves using fictional creatures as a proxy, yes. As ArcaneArts pointed out, if this were about <i>characters</i>, there wouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> I feel like I'm at a meeting of Sociopaths Anonymous. &quot;Last week I thought I'd find someone emotionally vulnerable and convince them to give in to their wrath. They nearly beat their partner to death. I watched. It was beautiful.&quot; I guess I could be more charitable in my interpretation and just find you all to be liars. Or I could apply Hanlon's Razor and decide you're all stupid. Do you have a preference?</div> </div> </div> </div>QFT.<br /> <br /> 100% agree with you. Beautiful post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T14:28:50-07:00","id":196557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=196088#post196088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Flexibility when it comes to doing your job for starters.<br /> <br /> The retirement package is also pretty competitive to boot.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... why not be unchained? Better to rule in Hell than be trapped in an eternal stalemate in the Supernal<br /> <br /> But yeah! I'm a little concerned about how some of these people are doing the shallow thing and judging people on their choices for a possibility that could never happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T19:16:15-07:00","id":196636,"title":"","content":"Let me clarify-I may have worded it strongly before, but I am far more baffled, with a small amount of being disturbed, by the <i>decisions</i> rather than the people. I like and trust the people here and generally hold a good opinion of you all. That, more so than my seven year old inside me, is why I find it so discordant that some people identify with the Pure or the Bale Hounds. I understand where the Pure are coming from, but I could never get behind it, and the Bale Hounds, well, they actively serve Vice itself. So seeing people I like and think of as good people with level heads and clear perspectives going with them is weird.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, I'm not worried about it. It's a fun mental exercise, a &quot;if I Changed, what then?&quot; sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <b>ON BEING A WEREWOLF</b><br /> <br /> I like other lines a lot more as a player, but there are four that, if they were real and I had some choice over being one but had to choose them, I would give serious consideration to. THose are Hunter, Mage, Sin-Eater, and Werewolf. As a werewolf you have a lot of issues to deal with, but they are neater and cleaner struggles, and personally more in line with experiences I have had. I place it last on the list, but being a Werewolf is a better state to be in than, say, a Demon, a Vampire, or a Changeling. If nothing else, the Oath of the Moon(and even, to a lesser degree, the Oath Of Urfarah) give you some pretty clear directives, something to direct otherwise idle hands. I don't prioritize being a Werewolf, I just acknowledge that of the many combos this'd be the one that fit me the most-I <i>could</i> Change into a werewolf and not be surprised one bit. The others might shock me more.<br /> <br /> EDIT: So, I quickly had a look over the Bale Hounds in Blasphemies when I got the chance to today, and, well, simply put the entire shebang ranges anywhere from pessimistic to fatalistic to nihilistic. I don't like pesmissim, fatalism, and nihilism. So, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-13-2014, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T19:49:54-07:00","id":196643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=196010#post196010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, of those who picked forsaken almost everyone went with Cahalith. I'm not surprised, but what is everyone's thought on this matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause I was curious, I went and counted this up. The first thing is that that are like, four or five people not in the Tribes of the Moon(I didn't properly count them), compared to fifteen in them. So, you know, contrast.<br /> <br /> The counts total(unless there are more on page 5, which I don't think there are):<br /> <br /> Rahu-3<br /> Cahalith-6<br /> Elodoth-3<br /> Ithaeur-2<br /> Irraka-2<br /> <br /> That is a <i>lot</i> of Cahalith, a lot more given how reserved the forums on the whole seem.<br /> <br /> My theory? Well, let's move away from the forums and look at the unifying factor-Werewolf itself. Werewolf may play the entire secrecy/shadows thing as much as anytone else, but they are definitely within the popular consciousness one of the loudest monster groups out there. THe Cursed from the FCG and the popular praise they received semi-reflects this, as the real kick from that cahracter type is when they explode into an unstoppable force that doesn't care too much about hiding-stalking, maybe, but even then that's to erupt from the shadows in terrible glory.<br /> <br /> I think by virtue of werewolves being werewolves, people who are into them tend to be people who sympathize more, whether positively or negatively, with wanting to let something rip out, with being louder than others. Those virtues draw people to the Rahu, Elodoth, and particularly the Cahalith.<br /> <br /> But that's a wild guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T22:39:04-07:00","id":196653,"title":"","content":"See, I was going to argue that the forums are more likely to house creative, artistic people than any other type of person. Story tellers, artists, and writers tend to be the Cahalith archetype, visionaries who channel their creativity into the hunt and their dreams into their art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T07:59:46-07:00","id":196786,"title":"","content":"That makes a lot of sense too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br 