ise they received semi-reflects this, as the real kick from that cahracter type is when they explode into an unstoppable force that doesn't care too much about hiding-stalking, maybe, but even then that's to erupt from the shadows in terrible glory.<br /> <br /> I think by virtue of werewolves being werewolves, people who are into them tend to be people who sympathize more, whether positively or negatively, with wanting to let something rip out, with being louder than others. Those virtues draw people to the Rahu, Elodoth, and particularly the Cahalith.<br /> <br /> But that's a wild guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Might want to recount that. I went back and racked up 5 Ithaeur.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I now see the point others were making on how this thread could be disturbing, thanks to Errol216's post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T09:14:33-07:00","id":196848,"title":"","content":"I counted only the Forsaken, since the question was on them explicitly. I know there were <i>way</i> more Ithaeur in general.<br /> <br /> Granted, I didn't explain why the Cahalith make a greater portion of the Forsaken populace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T09:36:02-07:00","id":196864,"title":"","content":"What do you mean? I was asking about all Werewolves, not just the Forsaken. Isn't Uratha the word they use to refer to their species? Like Kindred, or Lost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T09:38:50-07:00","id":196867,"title":"","content":"That's great, but the initial thing you referenced was in response to Nyx. Check out the quote in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T09:41:43-07:00","id":196868,"title":"","content":"ArcaneArts may be referring to Nyx's other question which directly relates to the Forsaken, &quot;<i>So, of those who picked forsaken almost everyone went with Cahalith. I'm not surprised, but what is everyone's thought on this matter?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Nyrufa's opening post referred to Werewolves in general. But we've since derailed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-14-2014, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T09:43:43-07:00","id":196870,"title":"","content":"Are Nyx and Nyrufa the same person? o_O<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nope, nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-14-2014, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T22:26:38-07:00","id":197551,"title":"","content":"I am me, I assure you.. Though who am I is a question I ask a lot.<br /> <br /> It seems to be an almost even split between Cahalith and Ithaeur as others have recounted. Rahu are a close third. My rationale for Cahalith is listed, but now I'm curious as to the why of the Spirit Masters. Time to re-read and think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T08:01:20-07:00","id":197932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=197551#post197551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am me, I assure you.. Though who am I is a question I ask a lot.<br /> <br /> It seems to be an almost even split between Cahalith and Ithaeur as others have recounted. Rahu are a close third. My rationale for Cahalith is listed, but now I'm curious as to the why of the Spirit Masters. Time to re-read and think.</div> </div> </div> </div>First instinct about the Ithaeur, the power trip and clarity of focus. Gaming houses a lot of creative people, but also a lot of folks looking for some kind of control and power over the world around them. While the blatant choice would be the Rahu for all the raging and killing, the Ithaeur are the ones who can control and influence the Shadow more naturally than anyone else. Also, the Rahu, Ithaeur and Irraka are probably the three Auspices with the clearest focus and intent of what they are: warrior, spirit-talker, sneak. Cahalith has developed the reputation as the loud story-tellers &amp; war-caller and a lot of people still aren't quite sure what to make of the Elodoth. When it's clearer what they do, it's easier to choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T09:12:20-07:00","id":197968,"title":"","content":"Things I see in this thread that I find to be not quite realistic:<br /> <br /> .) Tribes have standards. You can't call yourself a Storm Lord unless Winter Wolf actually accepts you as his own; and Rites of Passage can be quite difficult and exhausting and dangerous. It's not a math test, it could well be a fight for your life.<br /> <br /> .) There are too few Pure. Not because there are only very few people saying they <i>want </i>to be Pure (and keep those guys away from me, I don't want to see them or talk to them), but because the Pure are <i>very </i>good at what they do. Someone who has her First Change and is found by the Fire-Touched first will be a Fire-Touched or dead, barring extraordinary circumstances. People who brainwash know what they're doing, especially those with spirit magic to back them up. If you think you're not susceptible to brainwashing, you are wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T09:28:02-07:00","id":197973,"title":"","content":"What's up with pissing on people's parades. You can't argue realistically because we're talking about Werewolves in a game setting. There is no realistically. Someone says they're StormLords or Blood Talons then that is what they are. That is what they feel close to and have fun with. Arguing with them or putting them down for it is kinda silly. And the whole thing about someone who feels close to X tribe is dangerous or broken or psychotic is in the realm that someone who plays D&amp;D worships Satan or Vampire players of Goth blood drinkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T09:58:40-07:00","id":198015,"title":"","content":"1)Of course it's not real, I think everyone knows that. We're arguing about what we would choose if it were real and the uncomfortable implications that come with it.<br /> 2)No one is really arguing against the Tribes of the Moon.<br /> 3)It is perturbing when people associate with groups that promote racism, misanthropy, cruelty, hate, or a general support of the spreading of the worst of human instincts. It can indicate something with a person is wrong when they say they would join those groups. I don't think anyone is seriously screwed up, but it's worrying all the same.<br /> <br /> Let's clarify this again: we are talking about we, ourselves, as people, and what we think we would be as these fictional characters. Naturally a certain amount of leeway is to be assumed, but at the same time, there's also a clear choice at work here, and most of us have clear perspective on what these things mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T11:08:33-07:00","id":198060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=198015#post198015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's clarify this again: we are talking about we, ourselves, as people, and what we think we would be as these fictional characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're missing out on the big aspect of the question, which suggests that you are in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> \u200bChristian A got close to it, but he has some misconceptions about things like Death Rage (which aren't likely to pop up in every day life unless you're already harmony 1-2 and offering up your own flesh or those of others to spirits. most werewolves fall into the range of Harmony 6 to 7). And he didn't seem to appreciate that this is not us, now, with all the infinite possibilities our lives can take, as much as us, in the World of Darkness (which is generally considered worse, or at the least, darker, than our own world) having turned into werewolves, with all the infinite possibilities -that- entails.<br /> <br /> Your disapproving harping on the ways one would go with it is unnecessary.<br /> <br /> You don't like it, we get it. We can read, we saw you say so several times. Perhaps you can make another thread about it so other people won't be deterred from posting their own ideas by your criticisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T11:37:58-07:00","id":198082,"title":"","content":"Two things.<br /> <br /> First, this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not taking people too seriously here, or at least I'm working at not. It's just-it's less disturbing, more weird, that people choose to define themselves thusly. I still think really well of the people who have responded with joining &quot;el lado oscuro&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said this ages ago. I clarified it a little later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me clarify-I may have worded it strongly before, but I am far more baffled, with a small amount of being disturbed, by the <i>decisions</i> rather than the people. I like and trust the people here and generally hold a good opinion of you all. That, more so than my seven year old inside me, is why I find it so discordant that some people identify with the Pure or the Bale Hounds. I understand where the Pure are coming from, but I could never get behind it, and the Bale Hounds, well, they actively serve Vice itself. So seeing people I like and think of as good people with level heads and clear perspectives going with them is weird.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, I'm not worried about it. It's a fun mental exercise, a &quot;if I Changed, what then?&quot; sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that, and I meant that. Yes, it raises some uncomfortable notions, but I'm really not worried about it. I said as much in the very same post you quoted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone is seriously screwed up, but it's worrying all the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the entire subject had dropped last page, we had seriously moved on with it.<br /> <br /> Second, this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Original Poster, in the very first line,</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were to wake up one day and undergo the First Change, what kind of Werewolf would you become? This thread is to tell the rest of us!</div> </div> </div> </div>Has a small fight with this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And he didn't seem to appreciate that this is not us-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit though that this quote(not the poster)-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the whole thing about someone who feels close to X tribe is dangerous or broken or psychotic is in the realm that someone who plays D&amp;D worships Satan or Vampire players of Goth blood drinkers. </div> </div> </div>-kinda pisses me off, because it's not a fair comparison in context in the slightest, and hits on a hot button of mine.<br /> <br /> Look, I'm keen to move on, and I'm keen to stop caring that people choose the antagonists. We've gone through the rounds, I'm more or less satisfied. and last page, we seriously had moved on. And I'd like to see this go on. This entire thing has gone from a curiosity to a stupidly overblown thing(and yes, I know I helped it).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, is it really harping if the argument I ran with for the first half of this entire debacle is &quot;my inner seven year old doesn't approve&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-15-2014, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T12:28:26-07:00","id":198117,"title":"","content":"You know what I love about the RPing community? The fact that completely hypothetical and impossible conversations can result in this kind of backlash. I completely understand what Arcane is trying to say.<br /> <br /> &quot;I've got super powers! Time to kill some mother fuckers!&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, that would be kind of shocking to meet somebody who decided to flip the switch like that. But please, let's not let this get out of hand. My Kindred and Changeling threads haven't had any problems so far, but I guess that's because nobody decided to sign on with the Gentry or the Belial's Brood. But still, I'd rather not have this turn into a philosophical shit storm about the human spirit or the community's psychosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T14:09:52-07:00","id":198222,"title":"","content":"And no one picked to be one of the Unclean...How can you resist being a Wereroach..Pfft..Scuttling on peoples floors at night..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T15:17:18-07:00","id":198261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=198117#post198117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what I love about the RPing community? The fact that completely hypothetical and impossible conversations can result in this kind of backlash. I completely understand what Arcane is trying to say.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;I've got super powers! Time to kill some mother fuckers!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Yeah, that would be kind of shocking to meet somebody who decided to flip the switch like that. But please, let's not let this get out of hand. My Kindred and Changeling threads haven't had any problems so far, but I guess that's because nobody decided to sign on with the Gentry or the Belial's Brood. But still, I'd rather not have this turn into a philosophical shit storm about the human spirit or the community's psychosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is Werewolf, after all. Going about killing is somewhat implied. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T22:24:39-07:00","id":198560,"title":"","content":"If I'm completely honest with myself, I'd probably end up siding with the Fire Touched. I despise lies, while lying on a daily basis for the sake of my own survival. <br /> <br /> Also, I'd be very concerned about the implications for my newly-discovered-to-be-real immortal soul if the spirit brands of Auspice really do what the wolf god who's ban is that he can't stand lies spoken in his presence says they do. <br /> <br /> From their prospective they're on a crusade to save their fellow werewolves from an existence of suffering and slavery. Luna is acknowledged to be crazy even by the folks who follow her, and she already had the strike against her of being a psychotic diety who inflicts generation curses over crimes committed by someone's ancestors. <br /> <br /> The other Pure Tribes may not be great company, but they're also both on the outs in the long run. As humans populate more and more of the world, the Predator Kings can live in fewer and fewer places, and the rise of GMOs is going to be a death knell for them and their totem both. And the Ivory Claws are going to purify themselves out of existence. <br /> <br /> It isn't as though the Pure Tribes don't defend the people in their territories, drive off harmful spirits, protect humans from the hosts and generally do all the positive things we associate with the Forsaken including and especially fighting off the Bale Hounds and Maeljin incursions. <br /> <br /> All that said, I'd probably take a very long time to choose a side. I wouldn't want to make a less than fully informed decision, and that would result in me spending quite some time as a Ghost Wolf before eventually coming to Rabid Wolf's flock. After all, carving out an Auspice is both painful and permanent. I'd want to be really sure before making that commitment. Once I joined, I'd probably spend a lot of time on rituals and attempting to save the souls of my fellow werewolves by offering Rabid Wolf's truth to the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1764-cesario","name":"Cesario","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T23:42:47-07:00","id":198619,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, if there was a Pure Tribe I'd join, the Fire-Touched would be it. They're the closest to having theirs heads on straight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T01:40:41-07:00","id":198706,"title":"","content":"The Pure don't defend their own against harmful spirits. They serve those spirits. And they don't allow anyone to make an informed decision. That's not how their culture works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T01:42:19-07:00","id":198707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=198619#post198619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta say, if there was a Pure Tribe I'd join, the Fire-Touched would be it. They're the closest to having theirs heads on straight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as straight as can be expected for a tribe who follows a frenzied and maddened creature such as Rabid Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T02:34:19-07:00","id":198749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=198619#post198619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta say, if there was a Pure Tribe I'd join, the Fire-Touched would be it. They're the closest to having theirs heads on straight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's a good thing you are one of the Lost then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T03:00:41-07:00","id":198764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=198060#post198060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're missing out on the big aspect of the question, which suggests that you are in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> \u200bChristian A got close to it, but he has some misconceptions about things like Death Rage (which aren't likely to pop up in every day life unless you're already harmony 1-2 and offering up your own flesh or those of others to spirits. most werewolves fall into the range of Harmony 6 to 7).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is so biased it's hilarious. Go read the harmony rules. <br /> <br /> Your significant other wants to get you jealous. You'll catch yourself considering the person with which she wishes to induce that feeling as prey. Fresh meat. Harmony 5 and below starts to exhibit some neat crazy behaviors like bans. Y'know? because it's fun to anoint people you just met with your own blood sprinkles as if it was holy water. <br /> <br /> You get caught in transit tomfoolery, and subsequently get the urge to rip the fucker who cut you off throat's off.<br /> <br /> The one where most werewolves are at harmony 6 or 7 is particularly biased. How did you reached this conclusion? I wanna hear that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T03:20:29-07:00","id":198773,"title":"","content":"Well if this is what the Werewolf board gets like on weeks without Forsaken Friday, I wonder if I should offer some more playtest mutterings to stop all your rage and hunger turning inwards on each other <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T03:38:05-07:00","id":198778,"title":"","content":"Why do you think we're doing this? ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T04:45:45-07:00","id":198804,"title":"","content":"Hey, I could even give some actual play around how the new Gauru really works out in combat if everyone just chills out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T06:00:53-07:00","id":198852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=198619#post198619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta say, if there was a Pure Tribe I'd join, the Fire-Touched would be it. They're the closest to having theirs heads on straight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering they self-immolate, that's saying quite a lot about the other Pure!<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I went back and read the book and it doesn't say the Fire Touched are spiritually concerned or religious. It says they are Fanatics, and as such, that makes them infinitely more dangerous and unpredictable than the Ivory Claws or the Predator Kings. In the eyes of a fanatic, any crime is excusable as long as it serves their faith. Their gods will forgive them in the long run, and may even reward their dedication!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-16-2014, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T06:49:55-07:00","id":198890,"title":"","content":"The Fire Touched are fanatics who look forward to dying in combat against the Forsaken. Why wouldn't they? They go to Taga Dan - heaven - after death. Suicide missions are their modus operandi. Which tells you everything you need to know to understand their mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T08:00:23-07:00","id":198948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=198749#post198749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's a good thing you are one of the Lost then.</div> </div> </div> </div>So very true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:30:01-07:00","id":199034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=198773#post198773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if this is what the Werewolf board gets like on weeks without Forsaken Friday, I wonder if I should offer some more playtest mutterings to stop all your rage and hunger turning inwards on each other <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Damm, he saw right through our ruse! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrotazarim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I could even give some actual play around how the new Gauru really works out in combat if everyone just chills out</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll be good boys and gals, promise <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:02:53-07:00","id":199081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=198764#post198764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one where most werewolves are at harmony 6 or 7 is particularly biased. How did you reached this conclusion? I wanna hear that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 184 of Werewolf the Forsaken, in the Harmony section, where it details what every state of harmony is like.<br /> &quot;Harmony 7: Most werewolves fall into the range of Harmony 6 to 7.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for the rest my &quot;bias&quot; it was in the Death Rage section, starting at the bottom of page 173, where it details stimuli that cause werewolves to go into Death Rage out of combat, and from 5 to 10 you have taking agg damage outside of combat, loved one or packmate in danger, betrayal by an ally (this is not suspicion), and a loved one or packmate slain or badly injured, or betrayed by a loved one or packmate. A significant other trying to get you jealous would count more towards being humiliated or insulted or, if you're a particularly possessive person, having your authority challenged, which range way down there at 1-4 Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-16-2014, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:10:47-07:00","id":199091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=198890#post198890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fire Touched are fanatics who look forward to dying in combat against the Forsaken. Why wouldn't they? They go to Taga Dan - heaven - after death. Suicide missions are their modus operandi. Which tells you everything you need to know to understand their mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovely, we've got a bunch of werewolf Taliban. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T11:03:23-07:00","id":199121,"title":"","content":"If I was in the Pure I would probably have joined the Predator Kings, but I'd really prefer to join the Forsaken instead. But then again, if I became part of the Pure its not like what I want is going to matter much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T11:17:46-07:00","id":199127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199091#post199091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Lovely, we've got a bunch of werewolf Taliban. XD</div> </div> </div> </div> The Taliban were precisely the sort of people Matt McFarland was using as inspiration when he wrote the Fire Touched chapter of the Pure book. This is also the context in which I see posters who would see themselves as Fire Touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T12:01:33-07:00","id":199138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199127#post199127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Taliban were precisely the sort of people Matt McFarland was using as inspiration when he wrote the Fire Touched chapter of the Pure book. This is also the context in which I see posters who would see themselves as Fire Touched.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Got to agree with this.<br /> <br /> Its entirely possible for a Uratha to have a strong faith without being part of the Fire-Touched. Mother Luna, the Oath of the Moon and the Forsaken Firstborn all seems like things worthy to venerate far more than the Pure totems and spirit-gods. Especially when you get actual veneration and faith in something which isn't based on brainwashing.<br /> <br /> Just because the Pure does something loud and big don't mean that the Forsaken can't do the same better and more classy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T12:21:06-07:00","id":199146,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the Storm Lords are the tribe that lends itself the best towards character concepts with strong conviction and faith in what they do; but it takes conviction to join any of the Forsaken tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:07:01-07:00","id":199430,"title":"","content":"The problem with the Taliban comparison is that the Fire Touched are fanatics about honesty. Lying about the nature of the Lunes and Taga Dan is just as bad as lying about anything else in their worldview. I would believe of Luna that she enslaves the souls of the Forsaken upon their deaths, turning their renown brands into manacles that force them to obey her will. <br /> <br /> Luna is an inconstant, insane being from the outer darkness. She's powerful, yes, but power isn't why you offer your faith and loyalty. Besides, the hypocracy of venerating Luna when you scoff at the idea of venerating spirit gods. She IS a spirit god. <br /> <br /> The main thing Luna has going for her in terms of classifying her as worthy to worship is that the Bale Hounds have a huge hate on for her. That would be the one thing to give me pause, since the Maeljin are the most obviously evil things in the setting. Luna might be the lesser of two evils, which would explain why the Forsaken totems signed on with her, but I think there's something to the idea that being pure in your convictions, and keeping any necessary alliances with the lesser of two evils at arms length, and only so long as you're fighting the common enemy of the greater evil. <br /> <br /> The Pure establish alliances with the local spirits, but they don't do so blindly. They hate the spiritually damaged resonance of a wound just as much as any Forsaken. It's just the Pure recognize the wisdom in working with the powerful local spirits instead of against them in maintaining a beneficial status quo for all involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1764-cesario","name":"Cesario","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T18:26:01-07:00","id":199491,"title":"","content":"I suppose in a way the Pure have some similarities to the Demons of Descent. In that they rebel against what they see as a tyrant, and half their creator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T18:28:45-07:00","id":199494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cesario</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199430#post199430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the Taliban comparison is that the Fire Touched are fanatics about honesty. Lying about the nature of the Lunes and Taga Dan is just as bad as lying about anything else in their worldview. I would believe of Luna that she enslaves the souls of the Forsaken upon their deaths, turning their renown brands into manacles that force them to obey her will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fire-Touched propaganda to garner converts. Rabid Wolf is the weakest Firstborn, so he built the perfect cult in order to make the biggest tribe. There are cases of werewolves who've become Lunes, but those had been expressively a requested honor. In the specific example in the books, the character in question shed her mortal half in order to shed the pain of losing her child(s).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cesario</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199430#post199430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna is an inconstant, insane being from the outer darkness. She's powerful, yes, but power isn't why you offer your faith and loyalty. Besides, the hypocrisy of venerating Luna when you scoff at the idea of venerating spirit gods. She IS a spirit god.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Purity 4 Rahu Meninna recognizes she's insane. He's dealt with the insanity she produced in his Ithaeur elder, who embraces the Mad-Mother body and soul, but the thing with Luna? She's a <i>distant</i> God. Service is optional. Veneration is optional. She only laid down the Oath of the Moon, and the Forsaken had to prove they deserved it by displaying they could take up the Father's mantle.<br /> <br /> Fire-Touched who wish to convert a high Harmony Forsaken will resort at nothing short of brainwashing in order to do so. They'll feed only human hands to the unfortunate victim while she's locked away, piss on the flayed skin of her exposed silver brands in preparation to the Offering of Blood and Silver, and if the Forsaken proves to be incorruptible? use a silver knife to pull out her heart in an even more blasphemous rite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cesario</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199430#post199430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing Luna has going for her in terms of classifying her as worthy to worship is that the Bale Hounds have a huge hate on for her. That would be the one thing to give me pause, since the Maeljin are the most obviously evil things in the setting. Luna might be the lesser of two evils, which would explain why the Forsaken totems signed on with her, but I think there's something to the idea that being pure in your convictions, and keeping any necessary alliances with the lesser of two evils at arms length, and only so long as you're fighting the common enemy of the greater evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pure are a textbook example cynical, hate-bound group. Predator Kings keep people into breeding camps that would make your favorite crimes against humanity offender blush.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cesario</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199430#post199430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure establish alliances with the local spirits, but they don't do so blindly. They hate the spiritually damaged resonance of a wound just as much as any Forsaken. It's just the Pure recognize the wisdom in working with the powerful local spirits instead of against them in maintaining a beneficial status quo for all involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure do not choose their totems. Their Oath 'to Urfarah' guarantees that any spirit of higher rank than them will run the show. They'll breed their totem's brood into Ridden.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T18:38:57-07:00","id":199503,"title":"","content":"That actually makes perfect sense, Cesario. What makes her any different than the other spiritual gods out there? Just because she's mommy dearest? Seems like a pretty immature argument from her case. Also sounds a lot like something I've had personal experience with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T18:44:38-07:00","id":199517,"title":"","content":"Luna may be a batshit insane distant alien god-thing, but for all of that she has shown certain predilections towards at least keeping the status quo we're enjoying going on.<br /> <br /> The Pure and Bale Hounds aren't particularly hoping for anything of that sort for the world if they finally get what they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T19:46:41-07:00","id":199561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199503#post199503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes her any different than the other spiritual gods out there?</div> </div> </div> </div>She doesn't hate you as a matter of course, even if that's just out of sheer mercurial contrarianism. Her existence is a metaphysical near-constant that means she doesn't much care what you think of her or whether you worship her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because she's mommy dearest? </div> </div> </div>She is the mythic greatest-grandma to your entire extended bloodline, queen of half the hours on the clock, and the reason you're not flinching at the touch of fancy tableware. Even if your wolf-nature weren't already naturally inclined to defer to her position in the spiritual hierarchy, that's generally a being it's considered prudent to show at least token respect to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seems like a pretty immature argument from her case. </div> </div> </div>It also seems <i>exceedingly</i> immature to attribute arguments made on behalf of a distant night-goddess who has never spoken to her children outside of dreams and omens and intermediaries to a world-bending gestalt being whose brother is <i>the fucking Sun.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also sounds a lot like something I've had personal experience with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Seek professional counsel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T21:09:59-07:00","id":199609,"title":"","content":"Drop the mic man, Mr. Satchel left the building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T21:57:48-07:00","id":199670,"title":"","content":"That was rather civil, I see great progress <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, have to agree that Luna does make for a much better patron than most Incarnae aside from the Forsaken tribe totems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:02:15-07:00","id":199673,"title":"","content":"I imagine a lot of Incarnae are actually fairly civil as primal definitions go.<br /> <br /> I also imagine a lot of them are not exactly things I'd want to meet, let alone have yanking my chains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:14:29-07:00","id":199679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199673#post199673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine a lot of Incarnae are actually fairly civil as primal definitions go.<br /> <br /> I also imagine a lot of them are not exactly things I'd want to meet, let alone have yanking my chains.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to Satchel's response to Nyrufa actually ^^; ... but I could see what you mean.<br /> <br /> Well if you think about it, the Forsaken totems rarely &quot;yank the chains&quot; unless you somehow gain their attention and/or audience. The Pure totems are harsher task masters, but they seem to be roughly as non-intervention el as their siblings. They are all too powerful to afford that sort of attention on a single Uratha or a single pack for too long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:21:41-07:00","id":199682,"title":"","content":"I know, but I had to give a fair appraisal of the Incarnae all the same.<br /> <br /> As for the Pure, they tug harder because the Pure often just purely seek support against enemies. The Forsaken fought long and hard to earn the respect and devotion of the Firstborn, a trait that is one of the two main ways the Forsaken get totems.<br /> <br /> Doesn't hurt that the other way is sheer dominance. The Pure kinda seem like weenies in comparison, but you can't deny that becoming the whipping boy has perks-the Pure started out working to dethrone the Forsaken as the ruling power, and they succeeded.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Kinda makes me wonder what the shifting point was-when the Forsaken ceased being the top dog in the struggle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-17-2014, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:26:48-07:00","id":199686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199517#post199517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna may be a batshit insane distant alien god-thing, but for all of that she has shown certain predilections towards at least keeping the status quo we're enjoying going on.<br /> <br /> The Pure and Bale Hounds aren't particularly hoping for anything of that sort for the world if they finally get what they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>The status quo of the setting is this: There is no balance between the Shadow and the Flesh. Spirits constantly leak through cracks in the wall between worlds and have their way with humanity and the Flesh. It's a status quo that demonstrably doesn't work and is bad for the world.<br /> <br /> The Pure support this status quo. What's more, they encourage it. This is the world they want to live in, and everyone who disagrees absolutely needs to be annihilated at all costs.<br /> <br /> To be Forsaken is to strive for something better, to fight for a balance that wouldn't and couldn't exist without the Tribes of the Moon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:30:37-07:00","id":199687,"title":"","content":"That's clearly not the status quo the average person would experience-remember, most of humanity lives rather like we do, just withmore hints of things moving just out of sight.<br /> <br /> If the Luna, through the Forsaken, wasn't doing her job, it would look a lot like you describe it, and things would be a lot screwier.<br /> <br /> THey do though, and so most of the the average citizen goes through their life without being constantly screwed over by spirits.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's like civil(civic?) services-you'd know when you aren't in status quo when something keeps them from their job more so from when they do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:37:47-07:00","id":199695,"title":"","content":"It's the status quo from the point of view of the werewolf race, who tend to see more than the average person. To be a werewolf is to find some way to operate in the context of this status quo, either to support it, because it's easier and safer - that's what the Pure do - or to fight it and work towards something better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:39:24-07:00","id":199697,"title":"","content":"My point is, Luna and the Forsaken don't uphold the status quo. The status quo is terrible. The status quo is dangerous. The Forsaken are in it because they want something better for their territories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:49:01-07:00","id":199702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199682#post199682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, but I had to give a fair appraisal of the Incarnae all the same.<br /> <br /> As for the Pure, they tug harder because the Pure often just purely seek support against enemies. The Forsaken fought long and hard to earn the respect and devotion of the Firstborn, a trait that is one of the two main ways the Forsaken get totems.<br /> <br /> Doesn't hurt that the other way is sheer dominance. The Pure kinda seem like weenies in comparison, but you can't deny that becoming the whipping boy has perks-the Pure started out working to dethrone the Forsaken as the ruling power, and they succeeded.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Kinda makes me wonder what the shifting point was-when the Forsaken ceased being the top dog in the struggle.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though it has been hinted that the Pure will most likely be in the defense again sometime soon; they won't stay at the top forever. Having said that, the Forsaken would eventually be overthrown by the Pure again later down the line, then vice-versa forever and ever amen unless someone or something forced them to build a lasting peace ( unlikely) or one side completely destroyed the other ( even more unlikely).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:52:04-07:00","id":199703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199697#post199697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is, Luna and the Forsaken don't uphold the status quo. The status quo is terrible. The status quo is dangerous. The Forsaken are in it because they want something better for their territories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, see, my point is coming from a different angle. I'm talking about the status quo they create of most people when they do their thing, not what the status quo of reality without their interference is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T23:16:30-07:00","id":199711,"title":"","content":"The Pure are in power in 21st century US. They aren't in power in 21st century UK, among other places, and they havent been in power in 20th century US.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T06:48:42-07:00","id":199964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/192951-what-kind-of-uratha-would-you-be?p=199517#post199517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna may be a batshit insane distant alien god-thing, but for all of that she has shown certain predilections towards at least keeping the status quo we're enjoying going on.<br /> <br /> The Pure and Bale Hounds aren't particularly hoping for anything of that sort for the world if they finally get what they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mother Luna isn't crazy, she's just playing <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/XanatosSpeedChess\" target=\"_blank\">Xanatos Speed Chess</a> against multiple opponents at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:11:02-07:00","id":199986,"title":"","content":"A few notes:<br /> - Luna is an extremely powerful boundary god. Think about what he/she is guarding <i>against</i>.<br /> - The Pure really aren't nice people. The Fire-Touched <i>believe</i> their doctrine to be the truth, but that doesn't mean it <i>is</i> true. They worship a minor god of disease and madness, after all. The Ivory Claws are all about blood-purity and other unsavoury pursuits. The Predator Kings are a byword for brute force and savagery even amongst the Pure. They all believe they're in the right, but don't mistake that for meaning that they don't do terrible, terrible things on a regular basis.<br /> - 21st century UK is mostly under Pure control, apart from the major towns and cities and - of course - the moors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"l